    weight: 4,
    title: 'Floating Settlement Point',
    concept: `In a VPPA, the buyer receives the floating market price and pays the strike. The "settlement point" defines which market price is used — hub (regional aggregate), zonal (sub-regional), or nodal (project-specific delivery point). "Adders included" means whether ancillary service revenues, capacity payments, or other products are bundled into the settlement.`,
    whyMatters: `Settlement point selection is one of the most commercially important but often overlooked terms. Hub settlement insulates the buyer from nodal congestion. Nodal settlement exposes the buyer to location-specific price discounts that can be severe and persistent. The difference between ERCOT hub and a congested West Texas node has averaged $8–12/MWh in recent years — a material impact on net settlement economics.`,
