    whyMatters: `Non-economic curtailment is growing as solar and wind buildout outpaces transmission investment. In some ERCOT zones, non-economic curtailment regularly exceeds 5–10% of potential generation annually. Unlike economic curtailment (which at least correlates with low settlement prices), non-economic curtailment creates pure volume shortfall with no offsetting price benefit to the buyer.`,
