    concept: `The Interconnection Agreement (IA) is the contract between the project and the grid operator (ISO or utility) that gives the project the right to connect to the transmission system and deliver power. The IA process can take 3–6+ years and involves significant costs (network upgrade contributions). Where a project is in this process directly determines how "real" the project is and how likely it is to achieve COD on schedule.`,
